tools.description:
[shopper] Category Top Brands
Returns list of top-performing brands within a category, ranked by selected metrics.

**General Constraints:**
```json
{
  "pagination": "supports pagination (limit, offset, sort, asc)",
  "default_date_range": "default date range: last 28 days"
}
```

```ts
mcp__Similarweb__get_categories_top_brands(args: {
// Domain
//
// Amazon domain. Supported domains: amazon.com, amazon.co.uk, amazon.it, amazon.fr, amazon.de, amazon.ca. All category IDs, brands, and ASINs are domain-specific and must match the selected domain **Constraints:** domain and category are required
domain: string,
// Granularity
//
// Time granularity for the returned values **Constraints:** supports 'weekly', 'monthly'
granularity?: "monthly" | "weekly", // default: null
// Start Date
//
// Start date in 'YYYY-MM' or 'YYYY-MM-DD' format. For weekly granularity, automatically adjusted to the first Sunday of the specified month.
start_date?: string, // default: null
// End Date
//
// End date in 'YYYY-MM' or 'YYYY-MM-DD' format. For weekly granularity with MTD=true, automatically set to the latest available Saturday. For weekly granularity with MTD=false, automatically adjusted to the last Saturday of the specified month.
end_date?: string, // default: null
// Metrics
//
// Comma-separated list of metrics: total_views, total_views_share, units_sold, units_sold_share, revenue, revenue_in_usd, revenue_share, conversion
metrics?: Array<"total_views" | "total_views_share" | "units_sold" | "units_sold_share" | "revenue" | "revenue_in_usd" | "revenue_share" | "conversion">, // default: null
// Mtd
//
// When true with weekly granularity, end_date is set to the latest available Saturday. NOT supported for monthly granularity.
mtd?: boolean, // default: null
// Category
//
// Amazon category ID (numeric string, e.g., '679182011'). Category IDs are domain-specific and cannot be used across different Amazon domains. Use the category search endpoint to find valid IDs for your domain
category: string,
// Format
//
// Format in which the reply should be returned
format?: "json" | "xml", // default: null
// Limit
//
// Sets how many results to return.
limit?: integer, // default: null
// Offset
//
// Defines the number of results to skip
offset?: integer, // default: null
// Asc
//
// Orders the results by ascending or descending
asc?: boolean, // default: null
// Sort
//
// Selects a specific metric to order results by
sort?: string, // default: null
}): Promise<unknown>;
```

