Look up a domain's registration details via RDAP (the modern JSON replacement for WHOIS): registrar, creation/expiry dates, days until the domain expires, registrar-lock statuses, nameservers, and whether DNSSEC is enabled. Use this when a user asks who registered a domain, when it expires, why it 'stopped working' (an expired domain takes the whole site and email down), or to confirm the nameservers at the registrar match where DNS is actually hosted. Queries are made over HTTPS to the authoritative registry.

