`renew` and `purchase` (a one-name purchaseDomain) create a team purchase and return it in `data.purchase`, under the same rule as purchaseDomain: with purchasing power and `expectedTotalCents` the saved payment method is charged now, otherwise give the user `purchase.confirmUrl`. This also applies without X-Spacefast-Client. The registrar is asked only after payment; poll getDomainRegistration for the outcome. Released Spacefast CLIs before 0.9.0, identified by their capabilities header without X-Spacefast-Cli-Version, are never charged from expectedTotalCents: the purchase is held for a person, and the receipt adds the `checkout` pay link those CLIs read. Transfers require the `domains.transfers` feature. `transfer_in` checks the authorization code and registry locks, then creates a team purchase the same way, with the saved `contactId`; DNS stays unchanged. `transfer_out` queues unlocking and an authorization email to the registrant, then returns an operation. Only a current owner or admin of the domain's team transfers a domain out, acting as themselves; a team key is refused with `domain_transfer_forbidden`, and an agent grant asks its person first (`confirmation_required`). A domain registered, transferred in or moved to another registrant less than 60 days ago is refused with `domain_transfer_locked` and the lock's end in `details.lockedUntil`. Use the code at the gaining registrar. Email success means queued, not delivered; neither command acceptance nor unlocking proves completion. `resendAuthCode=true` explicitly requests another email after checking the inbox. Poll the registration transfer state for completion.

